            "title": "Will New Dividend And Higher Profit Outlook Change G-III Apparel Group's (GIII) Capital Return Narrative?",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "G-III Apparel Group recently reported lower year-over-year third-quarter sales of US$988.65 million and net income of US$80.59 million, while also recording US$1.61 million in asset impairments and updating full-year guidance to slightly lower sales but higher expected net income and earnings per share. At the same time, the company completed a long-running share repurchase program and introduced a new quarterly cash dividend of US$0.10 per share, marking a meaningful shift toward returning...",
